        ],
        "notes": "bind creates an explicit BoundFunctionObject carrying the target, bound this value, and bound arguments. The same representation covers generated functions, class/method/arrow objects, built-ins, and explicit built-in/host delegate adapters without expression-tree compilation or a bound-delegate metadata table. Calls concatenate common arities through JsCallArguments; construction ignores bound this, rewrites a self newTarget to the target, and preserves target constructability. Chained binding, name/length descriptors, lack of an own prototype, instanceof, and covered boxed/ordinary thisArg cases are supported. Remaining limitations are less-common realm/proxy/exotic invariants."
      },
      {
        "clause": "10.4.2",
        "feature": "Array exotic indexing and length behavior",
        "status": "Supported",
        "specUrl": "https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-array-exotic-objects",
        "testScripts": [
          "tests/Jroc.Tests/Array/JavaScript/Array_New_Length.js",
          "tests/Jroc.Tests/Array/JavaScript/Array_New_MultipleArgs.js",
          "tests/Jroc.Tests/Array/JavaScript/Array_Length_Set_Fractional_ThrowsRangeError.js",
