          "tests/Jroc.Test262.Tests/built-ins/Object/seal/JavaScript/object-seal-p-is-own-property-of-a-string-object-which-implements-its-own-get-own-property.js",
          "tests/Jroc.Test262.Tests/built-ins/Object/getOwnPropertyDescriptors/JavaScript/primitive-strings.js"
        ],
        "notes": "String.Construct creates wrappers with string data, a non-writable/non-enumerable/non-configurable length, and the requested prototype, including the new target's realm fallback. ObjectRuntime synthesizes enumerable, non-writable, non-configurable UTF-16 code-unit index descriptors; compatible definitions succeed and incompatible definitions are rejected. Own-key enumeration includes virtual indices, ordinary properties, and symbols in array-index/string/symbol order while filtering out the internal string-data key. String data is still stored under an internal-named descriptor rather than a fully inaccessible internal slot, so reflective isolation of that implementation key remains limited."
      },
